---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProblemsNav from '../../components/problems/ProblemsNav.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Contribute to AMDai"
  description="Guidelines for contributing to R9700 Lab Notes — cite, do not invent numbers, keep the static build green."
>
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <ProblemsNav current="contribute" />
    <h1 class="display mt-6 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Contributor guidelines</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      This site is independent living notes for local AI on consumer Radeon. It is not AMD.
      We would rather ship a TODO than a guessed tok/s.
    </p>

    <article class="prose-lab prose mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2 id="house">House rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Prefer llama.cpp over vLLM for consumers. Prefer Q5 over Q4. Q3 is estimate/community unless measured. Q1/Q2 stay off — including draft and MTP.</li>
        <li>Models from NVMe, not HDD. One LLM per GPU unless you deliberately combine.</li>
        <li>Do not reintroduce Qwen2.5 or Qwen3-8B. Abliterated stays educational.</li>
        <li>Do not invent flags, VRAM, RAM, or issue numbers. Mark gaps <code>TODO</code>.</li>
        <li>Official vs works: official means the SKU is on AMD’s current matrix or matching notes.</li>
        <li><code>HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION</code> is unofficial. Never present it as a plan.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="data">Edit data, not mythology</h2>
      <p>Most living facts live in YAML under <code>src/data/</code>:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>rocm-problems.yaml</code> — this tracker. Every row needs a last-checked date and an https source.</li>
        <li><code>errors.yaml</code> — troubleshooter patterns.</li>
        <li><code>stack-updates.yaml</code> — alerts matched to saved rigs.</li>
        <li><code>gpus.yaml</code>, <code>stacks.yaml</code>, <code>what-works.yaml</code>.</li>
        <li><code>bios.yaml</code> — chipset BIOS notes. Every claim needs an https cite or <code>todo: true</code>. Board rows are submissions only.</li>
        <li><code>data/runs/*.jsonl</code> — official <code>amdai-bench/run@1</code> cards. Seed only sourced tok/s. Credit the submitter. Do not invent a launch command.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Seed only what you verified. If you cannot open the GitHub issue, leave the row out
        or mark <code>todo: true</code>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="build">Keep main green</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>ACCOUNTS_ENABLED=0 FORUM_ENABLED=0 npm run build</code> must stay a static site.</li>
        <li>Do not import <code>src/server/*</code> from a page that prerenders when flags are off, except behind <code>if (accountsEnabled())</code> / <code>forumEnabled()</code> dynamic import.</li>
        <li>Add tests next to the lib you changed. <code>npm test</code> should stay green.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="voice">Voice</h2>
      <p>
        Plain English. No lorem. No “welcome to your app.” Cite with a real URL. Affiliate
        links are Amazon Associates, Rakuten, and B&amp;H only — see
        <a href="/disclosure">disclosure</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="translations">Translations</h2>
      <p>
        A translation is welcome if it does not drift from the English sources and keeps
        every TODO. Do not translate an invented number into confidence. ROCm’s own
        documentation translations belong in
        <a href="https://github.com/ROCm/ROCm">ROCm/ROCm</a>, not here.
      </p>

      <h2 id="conduct">Conduct</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/forum/rules">forum code of conduct</a> applies to comments on this
        site too. Argue the log. Abliterated is educational, not the default stack.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
